      "content": "it cut off right at the material part. anyway, you're mostly just saying \"this is a problem but technology will fix it.\" that feels like a bit of a cop-out. \n\nit's not just about tech improvements; it's about geopolitical reality. if we move away from stable fossil fuel markets and toward a system that depends on specific minerals controlled by a handful of adversarial nations, isn't that a massive strategic and economic failure in the making? i'm trying to figure out if the \"inevitability\" everyone talks about is actually a real economic forecast or just a convenient narrative that ignores these deep structural flaws.",
      "source": "evaluator"
